From 1067124e3ccf3a4343ec434b8762f88a09a9ad70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: llogen <christoph.lange@blindspot.software>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:40:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] persistent_data: restore the session timeout

bmcweb writes the session timeout as a non-negative integer, and the
JSON parser reads it back as an unsigned number. readData() asks for
a signed integer, gets no value and keeps the default, so a changed
SessionTimeout is lost at every bmcweb restart. Read it as unsigned,
as the revision field already is.

Tested: on the QEMU AST2600 EVB, PATCH SessionTimeout 1200 and then
Manager.Reset GracefulRestart or ForceRestart. Before this change,
bmcweb_persistent_data.json held the new value after the restart, but
SessionTimeout read 1800. With nlohmann_json 3.12.0, the value read
back from that file is unsigned: get_ptr<const int64_t*>() returns
null and get_ptr<const uint64_t*>() returns 1200.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: llogen <christoph.lange@blindspot.software>
---
 include/persistent_data.hpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/persistent_data.hpp b/include/persistent_data.hpp
index 51b7746..dac6a8d 100644
--- a/include/persistent_data.hpp
+++ b/include/persistent_data.hpp
@@ -196,8 +196,8 @@ class ConfigFile
                     }
                     else if (item.first == "timeout")
                     {
-                        const int64_t* jTimeout =
-                            item.second.get_ptr<const int64_t*>();
+                        const uint64_t* jTimeout =
+                            item.second.get_ptr<const uint64_t*>();
                         if (jTimeout == nullptr)
                         {
                             BMCWEB_LOG_DEBUG(
-- 
2.53.0

